---
// Santa Monica's Measure GS transfer tax, shown on the Santa Monica submarket page. Rates are the City
// of Santa Monica documentary transfer tax as listed by the LA County Registrar-Recorder (checked
// October 2026): $3.00 per $1,000 under $5M, $6.00 per $1,000 from $5M to $7,999,999.99, and $56.00 per
// $1,000 at $8M or more (the Measure GS tier, in effect since March 1, 2023). Each rate applies to the
// whole price, not just the part above the line. LA County's $1.10 per $1,000 is the same on both sides
// of every line, so it is left out of the comparison. Everything below is computed from these rules.
const LOWER = 5_000_000;
const UPPER = 8_000_000;
const rateFor = (price: number) => (price >= UPPER ? 0.056 : price >= LOWER ? 0.006 : 0.003);
const taxFor = (price: number) => price * rateFor(price);
const money = (n: number) => `$${Math.round(n).toLocaleString('en-US')}`;

const justUnder = UPPER - 1;
const underTax = taxFor(justUnder);
const atTax = taxFor(UPPER);
// The price at which a sale over $8M nets the same as one just under it.
const breakEven = Math.ceil((justUnder - underTax) / (1 - 0.056));

const tiers = [
	{ range: 'Under $5,000,000', rate: '0.3%', perK: '$3 per $1,000', example: `${money(4_500_000)} sale: ${money(taxFor(4_500_000))}` },
	{ range: '$5,000,000 to $7,999,999', rate: '0.6%', perK: '$6 per $1,000', example: `${money(6_500_000)} sale: ${money(taxFor(6_500_000))}` },
	{ range: '$8,000,000 and up (Measure GS)', rate: '5.6%', perK: '$56 per $1,000', example: `${money(9_000_000)} sale: ${money(taxFor(9_000_000))}`, gs: true },
];
---

<section class="section section-alt gs">
	<div class="container gs__narrow">
		<span class="eyebrow">Santa Monica Transfer Tax</span>
		<h2>Measure GS: Santa Monica&rsquo;s Own &ldquo;Mansion Tax&rdquo;</h2>
		<p>
			Santa Monica is its own city, so the City of Los Angeles&rsquo; Measure ULA does not apply here. Santa Monica has its own version instead.
			Voters passed <strong>Measure GS</strong> in November 2022, and since March 1, 2023 any sale of <strong>$8 million or more</strong> pays a city
			transfer tax of <strong>5.6% of the entire price</strong>. Below $8 million, the city&rsquo;s rate is 0.3% or 0.6%.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="container">
		<figure class="gs-cliff" aria-labelledby="gs-cliff-cap">
			<figcaption id="gs-cliff-cap" class="gs-figcap">One dollar over $8 million costs about {money(atTax - underTax)}</figcaption>
			<div class="gs-cliff__cards">
				<div class="gs-cliff__card">
					<span class="gs-cliff__label">Sold for</span>
					<span class="gs-cliff__price">{money(justUnder)}</span>
					<span class="gs-cliff__tax">City transfer tax: {money(underTax)}</span>
				</div>
				<span class="gs-cliff__arrow" aria-hidden="true"></span>
				<div class="gs-cliff__card gs-cliff__card--over">
					<span class="gs-cliff__label">Sold for</span>
					<span class="gs-cliff__price">{money(UPPER)}</span>
					<span class="gs-cliff__tax">City transfer tax: {money(atTax)}</span>
				</div>
			</div>
			<p class="gs-cliff__note">
				A seller needs a price of about <strong>{money(breakEven)}</strong> just to net the same as a sale at {money(justUnder)}. Anywhere between
				$8,000,000 and that number, the seller takes home less.
			</p>
		</figure>

		<figure class="gs-tiers" aria-labelledby="gs-tiers-cap">
			<figcaption id="gs-tiers-cap" class="gs-figcap">Santa Monica city transfer tax by sale price</figcaption>
			<div class="gs-tiers__wrap">
				<table class="gs-tiers__table">
					<thead>
						<tr>
							<th scope="col">Sale Price</th>
							<th scope="col">City Rate (on the full price)</th>
							<th scope="col">Example</th>
						</tr>
					</thead>
					<tbody>
						{
							tiers.map((t) => (
								<tr class={t.gs ? 'gs-tiers__row--gs' : ''}>
									<th scope="row">{t.range}</th>
									<td>
										{t.rate} <span class="gs-tiers__note">{t.perK}</span>
									</td>
									<td>{t.example}</td>
								</tr>
							))
						}
					</tbody>
				</table>
			</div>
			<p class="gs-source">
				Illustration only. LA County&rsquo;s documentary transfer tax of $1.10 per $1,000 is added at every price. Rates from the LA County
				Registrar-Recorder. Who pays is set in the purchase contract, so talk to your tax advisor and escrow officer about your own sale.
			</p>
		</figure>
	</div>

	<div class="container gs__narrow">
		<h3>What Measure GS means if you own a Santa Monica apartment building</h3>
		<ul class="gs-tips">
			<li>
				<strong>If your building is worth around $8 million, price it with the tax in mind.</strong> An offer of $8.1M can leave you with less than
				an offer of $7.95M. We run the net-to-seller math on every offer so you compare what you keep, not just the headline price.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Buyers price their own exit too.</strong> A buyer who expects to resell above $8 million knows the next sale carries the 5.6% tax, and
				that shows up in what they will pay today.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Most Santa Monica apartment sales fall well under the line.</strong> For a building under $5 million, the city tax is
				0.3%, about {money(taxFor(4_500_000))} on a $4.5M sale. Measure GS mostly matters for larger buildings and portfolios.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
